WEBVTT

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.050
His heart is completely gone,
but his vitals are normal...

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:25.750
What's going on?

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.920
An unknown assimilation phenomenon.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.340
And the others?

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.150
Yes... They all show different symptoms,
and there's no precedent.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.760
We don't even know if their lives are threatened.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.520
Lately, she'd been saying she
was sleepy all the time.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.630
I had no idea it was the Fafner's influence.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.550
This is our fault.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.530
We only analyzed the mechs, and failed
to anticipate any burden on the pilots.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.380
The same goes for me...

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.260
It always has, ever since her parents
were assimilated by their mechs.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:12.010
Sensei, this can be fixed, right?

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:15.800
I'll make sure they fix it. Don't worry.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.090
Okay.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.310
Looks like you still can't come out.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:29.310
Orihime-chan...

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.610
I'm sorry. I'll be able to leave soon.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.320
Let's go catch bugs again tomorrow, okay?

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.700
And go fishing and swimming in the ocean.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.220
Get plenty of rest.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.710
Tatekami Seri produces assimilation crystals,

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.730
Nishio Rina is comatose,

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.600
Kaburagi Sui's body mass has increased,

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.340
Mikagami Mimika has crystalline growths,

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.260
and Mikado Reo has lost part of his body.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.350
Are they all the Gordian crystal's effects?

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.970
The island is protecting their lives.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.730
As a result of preventing the original
assimilation phenomenon?

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.230
Yes.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:19.100
But it won't protect anything
other than their lives,

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.240
such as their human appearances or their minds.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:24.280
Their appearances or minds?

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.960
As long as they fight,
the changes cannot be stopped.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.130
They'll all take its blessing upon themselves.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.780
But in comparison to those
whose lives are unprotected,

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.250
they're brimming with hope.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.340
Isn't that right, Fumihiko?

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.980
Camp 3 located.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.940
Brigade control has given the order to land.

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.730
All right, this is as far as we go today.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.550
In five days, we've covered a
tenth of our planned course.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.240
This is going to be a long journey...

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.300
Once we get used to moving, we'll gain speed.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.080
This is still only a training period.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.080
All transport craft sighted.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.080
They arrived safely?

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.150
Send out a scouting party.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.840
Set up camp 4 at the twenty-kilometer point.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:44.020
Leave camp 1 behind.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.470
Have those people join camp 2.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:51.450
From this point on,
how many camps will we set up?

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.730
I wanted to go with Emery.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.190
You have to travel separately.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.770
That way, if one of you is lost,
the other will survive.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.220
I don't want that.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.490
Just to be on the safe side.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.050
I'm sure we'll all make it to
the place you two found.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.150
Start rationing the cargo.

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:15.370
Don't go into the town.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.490
The buildings are pretty old.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.870
They could collapse at any time.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.090
Mitsuhiro, Maya's heading out.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:23.380
We just got here!

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:36.890
This is Mark Sieben.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.650
I'm joining your scouting party.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:41.650
This is Raphael I.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:43.770
Thank you for coming.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.650
We'll drop down and begin recon.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.070
What is that?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.050
It was left by an enemy's large-scale attack.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:06:00.230
It's old now, so it should be safe.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:05.080
Whole cities and nations disappeared, just like this.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.410
All around the world, yes.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.180
Still, hope will not be lost...

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:13.780
No matter how many times it's taken from us.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:22.170
We keep three or four camps set up at all times,

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:24.760
while keeping 22,000 people on the move.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.860
It's a massive undertaking, but one that's
a hair's breadth from tragedy.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.460
There are people spread over a
distance of forty kilometers.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.500
Protecting them won't be easy.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.700
Moving faster increases that distance,
making them difficult to defend.

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:41.510
But if we shorten the distance so we can
defend them, we'll move more slowly.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.400
The general has a difficult decision to make.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.570
Yeah, the problem is where we should be.

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.190
The general's location.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:54.350
And the brigade control's location, forward base.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.710
I agree.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:59.130
That's where the scouting party's reports
will be received the fastest,

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:01.190
and we can deal with enemies at the rear, too.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.170
When do I go, Soushi?

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.380
When we receive word of an enemy

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.850
or when brigade control moves.

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.490
Can we protect them that way?

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:14.490
Want to go out on recon, like Toumi?

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:17.060
Her stamina is extraordinary.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.500
If we tried the same thing, we'd never last.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.370
All we can do is have faith in the scouting party...

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.510
It's the Human Army at our destination
that we should worry about.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.210
If they don't find out that the
enemy's been destroyed,

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:35.680
they could launch a bomb that'll blow us all apart.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.880
The thing they call "ROE Alpha"?

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:42.690
All we can do is believe that

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.860
the communication party dispatched
by the general fulfilled its duty.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.830
Incoming contact sign from Dhaka.

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.860
Send another message,
converted to a different code.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:06.750
If it's successfully received
again, our job is done!

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.340
Roger.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.720
Are...

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:21.230
you there?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.290
I-It's...

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:26.480
It's getting into my mind!

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.070
So they found us, after all?

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.810
Fenrir startup phase confirmed.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.660
Initiating fingerprint authentication.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:14.320
Damned monster's trying to get in my mind...

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:24.660
Too bad for you. I don't know
where the general is.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.370
If you want to read my mind,

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.960
you get all my rage toward you bastards, too!

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:32.960
Fenrir, execute.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:49.510
What's wrong?

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.650
Such powerful hatred...

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:55.550
It wants to keep eating until it finds our Mir.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.490
The Azazel-type that attacked the town?

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:00.480
No, it's a different one.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:03.240
The one that came to the town
has already been eaten.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:06.320
The one that ate it has grown much stronger.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:12.280
It's hard to believe.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:14.710
There's a second message, using a different code.

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:18.610
They destroyed the Azazel-type, then left Srinagar.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.680
They're currently moving this way
with several thousand citizens.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.220
Won't they bring the enemy with them?

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.160
They're traveling more than 2,500 kilometers.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.450
There's a good chance they'll encounter an enemy.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.370
What do you intend to do?

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:33.230
Send as much backup and relief as we can.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:36.230
Surely, headquarters won't declare ROE Alpha.

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:45.870
So what did the message Commander
Kamal received say?

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.370
They fought off the Azazel-type.

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.750
That's rich! What a laugh!

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.940
You believe that, Dustin?

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:58.590
The code conversion stopped in
the middle of transmission.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.840
Either an enemy got them or they used Fenrir.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.960
Then that means it's our turn.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:07.470
Prepare raid pointers and transport craft.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:10.120
This time, headquarters has
ordered us to retrieve them.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:12.230
The special models from D Island?

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.390
I can't believe we get to disassemble
the legendary mechs ourselves.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:17.530
What if Commander Kamal resists?

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.400
It's my job.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.870
ROE Alpha is absolute.

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:30.630
To save as many lives as possible,
I will fulfill my duty!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.810
These are all the rations we get today?

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:44.050
When I get back to the island,
the first thing I'll do is eat my fill.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.300
Then I'll take a hot bath.

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:48.950
Sounds awesome.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.060
Have you experienced being
on the side of the Festum?

00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.950
I haven't.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:02.010
I've only conducted partial-assimilation experiments,

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:04.760
in order to approach the Esperantos.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:05.570
Assimilation...

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.950
With the Mir's factor?

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.020
It was an application of the Makabe factor.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:13.730
But it only bestowed the power
to fight with Fafners.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:16.460
We didn't gain the power to
communicate with the Mir.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:21.530
Miwa-chan?

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:24.200
Miwa, calm down. It's okay.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.770
No. I'm scared, Emery...

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:31.950
Don't let their hatred swallow you up.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.480
Build a wall in your heart.

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:43.060
Someone's being attacked by the enemy.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:13.140
This is camp 3!

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.400
Camp 2 here! We have an emergency!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.980
Walter? What happened?

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.190
Is this Mitsuhiro?

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.650
Some vehicles heading your way
were attacked by the enemy!

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:22.860
What?

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.670
Report from camp 2.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:29.710
Several vehicles strayed off-course and
encountered a group of enemies.

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.040
Display their position.
We'll send a defensive force.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.040
What are they doing out there?

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.110
They wanted to get here quickly.

00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:42.050
But the sun went down, and they lost their way.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.050
Mark Sieben heading out.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.760
Toumi-senpai, I'm coming, too!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.970
Wait, Akira!

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:54.770
I'm going, too.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.100
Don't do it. Save your strength.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:59.150
People are under attack!

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.230
Do it to protect the people here!

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:36.790
There are people...

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.250
Don't!

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:20.980
You okay, Akira?

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:47.210
They had no power...

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:48.460
Why did you kill them?!

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:57.930
Don't waste your weapons.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:05.010
We have to conserve, or we won't be
able to fight when we need to.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.210
Akira...

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:28.250
Ai and the others will finish off the rest.

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:31.340
If we'd arrived five minutes earlier,
we could've saved them,

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:32.910
but there are no survivors.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:34.510
Let's retreat.

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.470
We aren't going to do anything?

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.820
Not even collect the things they left behind?

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:41.150
Another wave would come while we did.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.770
We'd lead the enemy back to camp with us.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:49.350
Then this is how you guys
have fought all this time?

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:50.870
It's enough that we can fight at all.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.780
The number of those who can't is far greater.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:55.860
That's true.

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:05.880
Did I leave the island just to see this?!

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:37.450
Damn. They're all moving too slowly.

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.700
Are they too scared of the assimilation phenomenon?

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:45.900
I guess it's natural to be scared...

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:23.870
The enemy is destroyed.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.150
Almost an hour after engagement...

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.870
That was a hard fight.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:32.590
It's watching.

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:33.480
What?

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.010
Response from Solomon!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:38.540
Azazel-type within the shield...

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:40.010
It's Walker.

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:46.470
It's gone.

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.450
Where will it appear?

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.400
It's laughing

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:55.400
at the soldiers from the island
who fear their own power.

00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:59.400
It's learned, Fumihiko.

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:12.690
It's growing.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:21.770
I feel so heavy...

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:24.990
Until now, I felt perfectly fine.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.190
No... There are more of them.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:46.780
Come on, how long have I already slept?

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.330
Damn it! Why am I so sleepy?

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:04.310
Thanks for the meal.

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:14.440
You suggest the introduction of
the unmanned trooper model

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:17.190
and the startup of Mark Dreizehn?

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.040
Yes.

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:20.830
They've cleared the exam stage.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:24.940
And you're aware of the high
probability of an unknown

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.200
assimilation phenomenon occurring?

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:28.890
If it does, we'll gain more clinical data,

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:31.540
increasing the chances of finding a way to treat it.

00:20:34.890 --> 00:20:38.770
The new assimilation phenomenon incorporates
and transforms parts of the body

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:41.050
in order to protect the pilot's life.

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.550
If we know how the assimilation
works, we can treat it.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.010
The Gordian crystal is the fundamental cause.

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:52.680
If we can analyze it...

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:59.710
Canon, you made this decision yourself?

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:00.980
Yes, Mom.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:04.470
But I won't be fighting alone.

00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:06.690
I have allies that are better fighters than I am.

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:10.370
I'll cover your shift.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:13.190
If you have any complaints or hopes, tell me.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:16.210
Thanks, Mom...

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:22.840
Sakura, you can no longer pilot
a Fafner as you once did.

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:25.470
I know I won't be of much help in battle.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.490
But I have to give those kids some courage,

00:21:29.430 --> 00:21:31.850
before they really can't pilot their Fafners anymore.

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:38.560
The Sleipnir system for controlling
the unmanned mech

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:42.010
can be linked with the weapons-control
operation immediately.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:48.080
Kaname Sakura... Hazama Canon...

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:51.620
I hereby acknowledge your return as pilots.

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:54.670
Prepare for deployment as per regulations.

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:10.470
Let's go! Believe in the mechs and in yourselves!

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:16.800
Every time someone faces a crisis,
someone else rises to meet it.

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:20.480
That was how we fought.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:24.260
Knowing that someone would be sacrificed,

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:27.650
we fought, believing we could protect someone.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:31.990
There was no other way.

00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.840
<i>Fafner in the Azure: Exodus</i>, episode 13:

00:24:09.600 --> 00:24:11.130
A Future Within the Darkness.
